    "title": "pandas.CategoricalDtype.ordered — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.CategoricalDtype.ordered#\n\n- property CategoricalDtype.ordered[source]#\n- Whether the categories have an ordered relationship. When `True` , comparison operations on the resulting Categorical\nare valid and sort in the order of the categories.See also \n  - `categories`\n  - An Index containing the unique categories allowed.\n Examples >>> cat_type = pd.CategoricalDtype(categories=[\"a\", \"b\"], ordered=True) >>> cat_type.ordered True >>> cat_type = pd.CategoricalDtype(categories=[\"a\", \"b\"], ordered=False) >>> cat_type.ordered False",
